1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,333
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,933
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:38,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,567
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,067
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:54,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:55,633
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:00:55,767 --> 00:00:57,267
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:02,567
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:04,567 --> 00:01:06,733
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:12,233
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:14,400
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,833
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:20,567 --> 00:01:23,533
[ENGINE REVVING]

17
00:01:25,433 --> 00:01:26,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:27,567 --> 00:01:30,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:31,433
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:32,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:34,200
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:36,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:44,400
<i>Someone could've died!
We overstepped, sir!</i>

24
00:01:44,533 --> 00:01:45,633
<i> Before you scold me...</i>

25
00:01:45,767 --> 00:01:46,933
<i> let's not forget</i>

26
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:50,500
<i>who ordered the demolition
in Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

27
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:51,800
<i> It's your father, isn't it?</i>

28
00:01:51,933 --> 00:01:53,233
<i>- Gentlemen!
- We exercised</i>

29
00:01:53,367 --> 00:01:54,433
<i> maximum tolerance.</i>

30
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:55,767
<i> But a civilian was shot!</i>

31
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,133
I don't know how you'll fix this

32
00:01:58,267 --> 00:01:59,433
<i> but you better fix it!</i>

33
00:01:59,567 --> 00:02:00,867
<i> She's looking for a job.</i>

34
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,467
<i>Your family committed
an offense against ours.</i>

35
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,833
<i>How bold of you
to even come to me.</i>

36
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:07,800
<i>Whatever happened between Gabo
and Django</i>

37
00:02:07,933 --> 00:02:09,033
<i> has nothing to do with me!</i>

38
00:02:09,167 --> 00:02:11,167
<i> Rudy just really needs it!</i>

39
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,933
<i>- For his funeral?
- For the hospital!</i>

40
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:14,533
<i>I have a meeting
at Jade Imperial.</i>

41
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:15,633
<i> The target is on his way out.</i>

42
00:02:15,767 --> 00:02:17,367
<i>- Visuals on target.
- Let's follow him.</i>

43
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,233
<i>Follow Mr. Chan.
I'll be right behind you.</i>

44
00:02:19,367 --> 00:02:22,167
<i>I'll just get my bike.
I'll see you at Jade Imperial.</i>

45
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:26,133
- [THUDS]
- [GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:26,267 --> 00:02:27,367
We're done for.

47
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,267
The issue's already reached
the higher-ups.

48
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,333
We wouldn't be having an issue
if it weren't for that Salvador.

49
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,167
What do you want, sir?

50
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:36,167
- Want me to get rid of him?
- No.

51
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,367
Not yet.

52
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,467
Eyes are still on us.

53
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,833
They'll blame us for sure
if anything happens to him.

54
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:45,667
Just give him a little scare.

55
00:02:45,967 --> 00:02:46,800
Huh?

56
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:48,100
So he'll learn.

57
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:51,100
Aye, sir. I'll give him
a little nudge.

58
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,867
- Umali.
- Yes, sir.

59
00:02:55,233 --> 00:02:57,000
Let someone else do it, okay?

60
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,767
I don't want to deal with
any loose ends.

61
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,133
- Copy, sir.
- Sir.

62
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:02,733
How about the other problem?

63
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:04,267
The civilian who got shot.

64
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,700
Send Lieutenant Jacinto here.

65
00:03:10,033 --> 00:03:11,733
If we're going to give someone
a scare,

66
00:03:12,967 --> 00:03:15,133
then we need
to coax someone else.

67
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:16,433
[LAUGHS]

68
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:18,133
Yes, sir.

69
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:25,267
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

70
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:35,233
Excuse me, sir.

71
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:37,533
You called for me?

72
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,100
Yes. Lieutenant Jacinto, please.

73
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:50,600
General Duran rushed here
because of the...

74
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,433
controversies about
the demolition

75
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,700
of Ginintuang Lupa.

76
00:03:54,833 --> 00:03:57,100
I didn't do anything wrong,
did I?

77
00:03:59,533 --> 00:04:00,533
Answer.

78
00:04:01,733 --> 00:04:02,600
No, sir.

79
00:04:02,733 --> 00:04:05,000
I just followed
your father's orders.

80
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:08,133
And because of that, it could
affect my career.

81
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:11,133
Do you think I deserve that,
Lieutenant Jacinto?

82
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,267
Answer.

83
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,667
No, sir.

84
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:20,167
You don't deserve that.

85
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:22,967
I just followed orders
because I am a good soldier

86
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:24,233
and now...

87
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,800
I'm the one getting caught
in the middle of it all.

88
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,233
I couldn't do anything.

89
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,400
Is there anything...

90
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,033
that you or your family could do

91
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:37,500
to prevent the situation
from blowing up

92
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,333
[DOMINGO SIGHS]

93
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:40,800
even more?

94
00:04:40,933 --> 00:04:47,933
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:53,633
I understand, sir.

96
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:56,433
You don't deserve this.

97
00:04:58,933 --> 00:05:01,433
So I want to pay you back
for the favor you did

98
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,867
for my father.

99
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,033
Thank you, Lieutenant Jacinto.

100
00:05:07,433 --> 00:05:08,567
Thank you.

101
00:05:13,067 --> 00:05:14,133
Ma'am.

102
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,200
[SIGHS]

103
00:05:17,333 --> 00:05:18,300
[DOOR CLOSES]

104
00:05:19,467 --> 00:05:21,133
[CHAIR SCRAPING]

105
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:23,333
[SIGHS]

106
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:25,200
Ma'am, are you alright?

107
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:26,967
You seem troubled.

108
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,633
Did the Colonel say anything?

109
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,633
Colonel Domingo was scolded
by General Duran

110
00:05:31,767 --> 00:05:33,200
for that viral interview.

111
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:36,333
The Colonel was the one
who got scolded,

112
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,933
but why do you look bothered?

113
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:39,800
I was just thinking...

114
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,933
Our unit is the reason why

115
00:05:44,067 --> 00:05:47,700
the image of NLEA
is being ruined.

116
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:51,233
So you know, even if it's wrong,

117
00:05:52,733 --> 00:05:56,433
I have to help Colonel Domingo
with this problem.

118
00:05:57,433 --> 00:06:03,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:06:04,733 --> 00:06:05,767
Hey.

120
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,833
It's Tonyo!

121
00:06:10,233 --> 00:06:12,733
- Tonyo!
- Hi, Tonyo!

122
00:06:12,867 --> 00:06:13,900
Gosh.

123
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:16,167
He's stingy with money.

124
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,700
It's better than nothing.

125
00:06:17,833 --> 00:06:19,833
Tonyo, will you book
a table with us?

126
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:22,967
I am looking
for a good meal.

127
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,367
- Oh!
- But...

128
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,267
It seems like the food here
is spoiled.

129
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,767
Watch how you speak!
Take a look t yourself!

130
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:33,233
You went here drunk,
but not with our drinks!

131
00:06:33,367 --> 00:06:35,867
I'm trying to save money!

132
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:39,700
I came here drunk so you'll all
look beautiful in my eyes

133
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:41,767
But I don't think it worked.

134
00:06:41,933 --> 00:06:43,600
Wow!

135
00:06:43,733 --> 00:06:46,000
Look at you, Tonyo!

136
00:06:46,133 --> 00:06:49,300
I'll pray for you
so you look more handsome!

137
00:06:49,433 --> 00:06:50,933
He's hopeless.

138
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:54,000
Betchay, you don't look
spoiled at all.

139
00:06:54,433 --> 00:06:55,700
You're stale!

140
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:57,300
[LAUGHTER]

141
00:06:57,433 --> 00:06:59,167
Fine, I'll get a table with you.

142
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,467
Now we're talking!

143
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,533
Tonyo!

144
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,133
Shh! Aya!

145
00:07:07,633 --> 00:07:09,167
[ISOBEL GASPS] Twinkle!

146
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,333
- That should already be set up.
- Yes, ma'am.

147
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:17,600
- Mom.
- Oh!

148
00:07:17,733 --> 00:07:19,067
- Hi.
- Max.

149
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,700
- Hi, Mom.
- Hmm.

150
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,533
How's work?

151
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:27,433
I want to say its okay,

152
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:29,200
but it's not.

153
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:32,200
It's because of the people
in Ginintuang Lupa.

154
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,533
Oh my God.

155
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:36,533
They already filed for a TRO
to stop the demolition.

156
00:07:36,667 --> 00:07:38,833
I mean, what other
countermeasure do they need?

157
00:07:38,967 --> 00:07:41,267
Dad, you don't have
to worry about this.

158
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,900
But I want to let you know

159
00:07:44,033 --> 00:07:46,800
that I'm going to settle
with the victim's family.

160
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,567
Um...

161
00:07:48,733 --> 00:07:51,000
Max, that place is dangerous.

162
00:07:51,133 --> 00:07:54,100
My people are already moving
to fix the problem.

163
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:58,167
And we will not settle
with anyone.

164
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:01,467
Dad, let me do this
for the family.

165
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,900
Especially for you.

166
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:04,100
[ISOBEL] Max.

167
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,767
If you have a solution
and you're planning to go there,

168
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,333
just don't let them know
that you're a cop.

169
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:11,567
Or a Jacinto.

170
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,900
You'll surely get in trouble.

171
00:08:16,567 --> 00:08:17,833
Mom.

172
00:08:17,967 --> 00:08:22,133
At least, just...
let me talk to that woman.

173
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:25,200
The one in the news.
She's ruining our reputation.

174
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:27,700
Including our family-- our name!

175
00:08:27,833 --> 00:08:30,567
What woman on the news?
What are you talking about, Max?

176
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:33,233
[TWINKLE] Ma'am Max,
I know about her!

177
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:35,667
She's doing too much!
I saw her on the news.

178
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:38,633
- She just wants to be viral.
- Exactly.

179
00:08:38,767 --> 00:08:39,967
Wait. I'm lost.

180
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:42,133
Who's this girl
you're talking about?

181
00:08:42,267 --> 00:08:43,100
What is this?

182
00:08:43,233 --> 00:08:45,167
[MAX] Haven't you seen
the news, Mom?

183
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:47,333
Toto and I have seen it.

184
00:08:47,467 --> 00:08:49,133
Where? Let me see it.

185
00:08:49,267 --> 00:08:51,233
- Show it to them.
- Toto!

186
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:53,133
Toto!

187
00:08:53,433 --> 00:08:55,300
- Sweetie...
- Hurry up!

188
00:08:55,467 --> 00:08:58,433
- Sweetie.
- Show it to sir!

189
00:08:58,567 --> 00:09:00,733
- Hurry!
- Let me see. C'mon.

190
00:09:03,233 --> 00:09:05,300
- Here you go, sir.
- What's that? Let me see.

191
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:09,667
[SALVADOR] After we interviewed
a woman whose husband,

192
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,233
<i> Rudy Magtibay,</i>

193
00:09:11,367 --> 00:09:14,900
<i>is currently in critical
condition at the hospital.</i>

194
00:09:15,133 --> 00:09:17,633
<i>One question remains
in the family's mind,</i>

195
00:09:17,633 --> 00:09:19,267
<i> who fired the shot?</i>

196
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,900
<i> Who is to blame for this?</i>

197
00:09:21,033 --> 00:09:23,000
We will never stop pursuing this

198
00:09:23,133 --> 00:09:26,800
<i>until whoever is responsible
is held accountable.</i>

199
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:29,967
<i>This is Salvador
"Benggador" Manalo.</i>

200
00:09:30,667 --> 00:09:33,300
<i>Standing by the oppressed.
This is Telebalita.</i>

201
00:09:34,033 --> 00:09:36,800
[ISOBEL] How dare they!

202
00:09:37,933 --> 00:09:41,000
What's all this fuss
when they're in the wrong?!

203
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,533
[MAX] Exactly, Ma.

204
00:09:42,667 --> 00:09:45,200
So let me do this because
this woman won't stop.

205
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,400
She's looking for money
so she can shut up.

206
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:52,433
- And you, Twinkle. Come here.
- Ma'am.

207
00:09:52,567 --> 00:09:56,600
Next time you hear any
news about us,

208
00:09:56,733 --> 00:09:58,133
let us know right away!

209
00:09:58,267 --> 00:09:59,233
Yes, ma'am.

210
00:10:03,467 --> 00:10:10,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:10:13,667 --> 00:10:15,767
You're lucky you survived, Rudy.

212
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,967
<i>But karma will surely
get you back.</i>

213
00:10:20,967 --> 00:10:25,300
<i>I myself will ensure that you
and your loved ones</i>

214
00:10:26,167 --> 00:10:27,600
<i>pay for the wrongs
you've done to me.</i>

215
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:28,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:32,000
Hey, one bottle of beer please!

217
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:34,567
Don't you want
to order any bar chow?

218
00:10:34,733 --> 00:10:36,167
Not even fish crackers
or peanuts?

219
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,800
Let me tell you this,
the best bar chow

220
00:10:38,933 --> 00:10:39,967
is conversations.

221
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:41,667
Anything you want to share?

222
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:43,167
Conversation? [SCOFFS]

223
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,467
[CLEARS THROAT] Okay.

224
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,567
[SPEAKERS PLAYING
DOWNBEAT MUSIC]

225
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:46,967
- It's about Rudy--
- Oh!

226
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,100
I'm done.

227
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,867
I'm bored
with your story already.

228
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,633
I haven't even said a thing!

229
00:10:51,767 --> 00:10:52,667
I got an idea.

230
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,133
Just dance.

231
00:10:55,267 --> 00:10:58,000
You want me to dance?
I only had one beer.

232
00:10:58,133 --> 00:11:00,367
Oh, please, you're crazy.

233
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:03,567
Fine then.
I'll sing and you'll dance.

234
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,700
No, Tonyo, no.

235
00:11:04,833 --> 00:11:06,067
- Let's just talk.
- Come on.

236
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,267
- I'll sing. Miss! Miss!
- Tonyo!

237
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,033
- Hey! Go back here!
- Can I borrow a mic?

238
00:11:10,167 --> 00:11:11,200
I'll tell you a story!

239
00:11:11,333 --> 00:11:12,300
This one's for you!

240
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
- [BETCHAY] Shhh!
- [TONYO SINGING] Betchay

241
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:19,600
<i> - Your thighs are so thick
</i>- Stop singing.

242
00:11:19,733 --> 00:11:21,733
[TONYO]
<i> Your legs are full of veins</i>

243
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:24,600
[BETCHAY] Enough! Shhh!
Let's just talk.

244
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:27,300
Tonyo, please!
Fine, I'll dance.

245
00:11:27,433 --> 00:11:29,133
Just stop singing. There.

246
00:11:30,167 --> 00:11:32,000
Put some energy into it!

247
00:11:32,867 --> 00:11:34,133
You know what, I'm done.

248
00:11:34,267 --> 00:11:35,300
No, no, please don't.

249
00:11:35,433 --> 00:11:36,900
- Aya!
- [AYA] What?

250
00:11:37,033 --> 00:11:38,133
[TONYO] Aya!

251
00:11:38,267 --> 00:11:39,600
- Why?
- [TONYO] Let's go!

252
00:11:39,733 --> 00:11:42,200
Baby, come to papa!

253
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:43,833
- Come on.
- Let's go.

254
00:11:43,967 --> 00:11:45,133
Give me a good time.
Betchay is useless.

255
00:11:45,267 --> 00:11:46,400
Absolutely!

256
00:11:46,533 --> 00:11:48,367
- [TONYO] Where should we go?
- [AYA] Oh, let's go there.

257
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,533
I'll give you
a good time, darling.

258
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:52,033
What happened?

259
00:11:52,267 --> 00:11:54,667
Oh, Tonyo is such a pain
to deal with!

260
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,733
You're good.
That's just the way it is.

261
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:59,333
When they're drunk,
they're easy.

262
00:11:59,467 --> 00:12:01,633
It's okay.
More men are coming, right?

263
00:12:02,067 --> 00:12:03,167
For sure.

264
00:12:04,667 --> 00:12:05,633
Betchay!

265
00:12:05,767 --> 00:12:07,433
Oh, Paquito, sorry!

266
00:12:08,367 --> 00:12:09,767
That wasn't my fault.

267
00:12:10,067 --> 00:12:11,533
Please give me another chance--

268
00:12:11,667 --> 00:12:12,633
Sit down.

269
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,667
We'll talk.

270
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,300
[PAQUITO GRUNTS]

271
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,700
Why did you ask me to sit?

272
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:24,500
I want you to keep me company.

273
00:12:24,933 --> 00:12:25,900
Don't you want to?

274
00:12:26,033 --> 00:12:27,967
You're making fun of me.

275
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,767
You're unbelievable.

276
00:12:30,233 --> 00:12:33,300
You know I'm desperate,
and you're making fun of me.

277
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:34,700
You're unbelievable, Paquito.

278
00:12:34,933 --> 00:12:37,467
I know you're not the problem

279
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:39,767
as to why no customer wants you.

280
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,300
It's on the customer.

281
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:46,467
I need money,
not someone to talk to.

282
00:12:47,133 --> 00:12:48,067
Hmm.

283
00:12:48,433 --> 00:12:49,800
You need money, you say?

284
00:12:50,467 --> 00:12:51,400
There.

285
00:12:52,167 --> 00:12:53,200
You can have that.

286
00:12:54,967 --> 00:12:56,233
- Really?
- Yes.

287
00:13:00,033 --> 00:13:01,300
You know what, Betchay...

288
00:13:01,433 --> 00:13:02,800
[BOTTLE CAP CLICKS]

289
00:13:03,033 --> 00:13:05,000
I've liked you for a long time.

290
00:13:06,433 --> 00:13:09,233
I've liked you
since we were young.

291
00:13:09,967 --> 00:13:13,200
The problem was that
Rudy made a move on you first.

292
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:17,233
What did you even see
in that guy?

293
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:19,800
For me, he's handsome.

294
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:22,800
You picked him. Now what?

295
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,033
He brought you misfortune.

296
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,767
And you have a stepson
who's an ex-convict.

297
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,467
You are with a man

298
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,133
who has achieved
nothing in life.

299
00:13:32,433 --> 00:13:33,500
Tell me.

300
00:13:33,633 --> 00:13:35,867
Is there anyone here
in Ginintuang Lupa

301
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,733
who has been successful?

302
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:38,967
Me.

303
00:13:39,867 --> 00:13:41,967
Betchay, I'm the king
of this place.

304
00:13:42,267 --> 00:13:44,167
I've passed the throne
to Django.

305
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:47,600
The problem is your stepson,
Gabo, wants that title too.

306
00:13:47,733 --> 00:13:48,867
Tell him off.

307
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,233
Because when our paths cross,

308
00:13:51,867 --> 00:13:53,167
I won't go easy on him.

309
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:54,633
[BETCHAY SCOFFS]
Leave me out of that.

310
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,967
Do whatever you want to him.

311
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:59,633
He's such a pain to Rudy and me.
He's a troublemaker.

312
00:13:59,767 --> 00:14:00,567
Really?

313
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,467
You're giving me permission

314
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:06,767
to beat up Gabo
until he turns purple?

315
00:14:07,133 --> 00:14:08,500
Why do you need to ask me?

316
00:14:08,633 --> 00:14:10,067
I thought you're a thug?

317
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:12,467
You're right.

318
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,467
Let's... let's just drink.

319
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,467
I'm paying.

320
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:18,200
[BOTTLES CLINK]

321
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:24,467
[FIREWORKS WHOOSHING, CRACKING]

322
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:30,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:14:31,067 --> 00:14:32,100
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

324
00:14:34,633 --> 00:14:35,800
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

325
00:14:46,733 --> 00:14:47,900
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

326
00:15:04,467 --> 00:15:05,567
[SEBASTIAN]
<i> We're about to go in.</i>

327
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,467
<i>Make sure
everything goes smoothly.</i>

328
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,833
Sure, sure.
We'll take care of it.

329
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:11,767
- [DIGITAL TRILLING]
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

330
00:15:12,767 --> 00:15:14,733
That's the place.

331
00:15:14,967 --> 00:15:15,933
That one.

332
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:20,933
Come on, come on.

333
00:15:22,067 --> 00:15:23,633
- Where's your invitation, sir?
- What?

334
00:15:23,767 --> 00:15:25,333
[BONG] Invitation?
Is it someone's birthday?

335
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:27,333
- [BOUNCER] Here, it's this.
- Don't you remember me?

336
00:15:27,467 --> 00:15:30,400
Sir, ma'am, you need to have
a QR code to get in.

337
00:15:30,533 --> 00:15:33,233
Here, here.
They're with me...

338
00:15:33,733 --> 00:15:40,733
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

339
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,567
Mr. Chan, welcome back!

340
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,333
The usual. Expensive.

341
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:50,533
Right away, sir.

342
00:16:08,833 --> 00:16:12,000
Mr. Chan, you can wait
and relax here.

343
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:16,467
Put the box there.

344
00:16:18,133 --> 00:16:20,267
Have a seat.
Make yourself at home.

345
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,767
[CAR APPROACHING]

346
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:31,000
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

347
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,800
[TEKLA] Hey! Say sorry!

348
00:16:43,233 --> 00:16:45,000
[BOUNCER]
You're bothering the guests.

349
00:16:45,133 --> 00:16:46,700
[TOLITS]
There's no one coming in!

350
00:16:46,833 --> 00:16:49,133
What's the problem?
What's the problem?

351
00:16:51,167 --> 00:16:52,100
[IPE] We got here first.

352
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:53,833
[BINOY] What's the thing
they're showing?

353
00:16:53,967 --> 00:16:55,500
[SCANNER BEEPS, CHIMES]

354
00:16:55,633 --> 00:16:57,833
[BINOY] It's not working!
Accommodate us first!

355
00:16:58,667 --> 00:17:00,033
[SEBASTIAN]
The QR code isn't working?

356
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:02,500
- Fix it! Hurry up!
- I'm trying!

357
00:17:02,933 --> 00:17:04,433
- I'm working on it.
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

358
00:17:04,567 --> 00:17:05,733
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

359
00:17:05,867 --> 00:17:07,500
- [MONITOR BEEPS]
- All good.

360
00:17:07,633 --> 00:17:09,033
Here, try it again.

361
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:10,900
[SCANNER BEEPS]

362
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:13,933
[EXHALES]

363
00:17:15,567 --> 00:17:16,967
- Thank you.
- We're actually with them.

364
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,567
[BINOY]
Can we share a table with you?

365
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:25,633
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

366
00:17:37,567 --> 00:17:39,233
[SEBASTIAN]
<i> We'll look for Mr. Chan.</i>

367
00:17:39,367 --> 00:17:42,167
<i>Alert us
once you see Tiger, okay?</i>

368
00:17:45,467 --> 00:17:47,067
Let's split up.

369
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,333
We'll check upstairs.
Let's go.

370
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:58,700
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,567
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

372
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:06,200
- [TOLITS] Gabo is here.
- [DABOY] There he is.

373
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:08,000
- [BONG] Gabo!
- [BINOY] Gabo!

374
00:18:08,133 --> 00:18:09,200
- Gabo.
- Gabo.

375
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:12,000
Well? Did you follow
Mr. Chan?

376
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:14,667
- We couldn't get in.
- Why?

377
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,300
We need the "QT"
to get inside.

378
00:18:17,433 --> 00:18:20,500
- Silly! It's QR, not QT!
- That's what I heard.

379
00:18:20,633 --> 00:18:22,400
We need to get inside.

380
00:18:22,567 --> 00:18:24,033
Tiger could be inside.

381
00:18:24,167 --> 00:18:26,400
What should we do now?
What's your plan?

382
00:18:28,667 --> 00:18:33,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

383
00:18:33,667 --> 00:18:34,833
Follow me.

384
00:18:37,267 --> 00:18:41,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

385
00:18:41,933 --> 00:18:43,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

386
00:18:46,433 --> 00:18:47,700
[HELMET STRAP CLICKS]

387
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:50,633
Let's split up.

388
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:53,400
Find a way to get inside.
We'll meet upstairs.

389
00:18:53,533 --> 00:18:54,700
Be careful, Gabo.

390
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,733
- This way!
- Let's go!

391
00:18:58,867 --> 00:19:05,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

392
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:21,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

393
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:35,200
[METAL CLINKING]

394
00:19:36,867 --> 00:19:37,833
[GABO GRUNTS]

395
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:49,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

396
00:19:53,633 --> 00:19:55,900
[CLOTHES RUSTLING]

397
00:19:56,367 --> 00:19:57,933
- [TEKLA GASPS] Hide!
- Hey!

398
00:19:57,933 --> 00:19:59,233
- Take cover!
- Hide!

399
00:19:59,233 --> 00:20:01,433
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:02,900
How do we get inside?

401
00:20:02,933 --> 00:20:04,433
- Yeah.
- We're doomed.

402
00:20:04,967 --> 00:20:06,900
Look at us. We look like
we've been through hell.

403
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,133
Hey, speak for yourself!
Don't involve me!

404
00:20:09,133 --> 00:20:10,667
I've found us a solution.

405
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:11,700
What?

406
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:12,800
Right there!

407
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:15,100
What, the washing machine?

408
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:16,867
- Huh?
- No.

409
00:20:16,867 --> 00:20:17,933
I mean, that!

410
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:19,867
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

411
00:20:19,867 --> 00:20:21,067
- [DABOY] Tekla!
- What?

412
00:20:21,067 --> 00:20:22,633
- You take care of it!
- Stay quiet, okay?

413
00:20:22,633 --> 00:20:23,633
Yeah.

414
00:20:25,467 --> 00:20:26,967
[WHISPERS] Stay out of sight!

415
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:30,067
Hi, handsome!

416
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:31,800
- [GASPS]
- [GIGGLES]

417
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:34,367
Poor you.
Are you working all alone?

418
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:36,133
- Yeah.
- Will you fold all of this?

419
00:20:36,167 --> 00:20:37,667
Want me to help you?

420
00:20:37,667 --> 00:20:38,733
Okay.

421
00:20:38,733 --> 00:20:40,933
[TEKLA] You know, you're exactly
my type of guy.

422
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:42,900
- [TOLITS WHISPERS] Let's go!
- A hardworking man.

423
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:44,367
- [MAN] Oh, really?
- [TEKLA] Totally!

424
00:20:45,467 --> 00:20:46,500
[TEKLA SIGHS SOFTLY]

425
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,933
Come on, handsome.

426
00:20:47,933 --> 00:20:49,600
Let's fold them all together.

427
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,033
- Sure thing.
- I'll help you.

428
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:53,733
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [TEKLA GIGGLING]

429
00:20:53,733 --> 00:20:54,733
Hey!

430
00:20:54,733 --> 00:20:55,933
Let's go!

431
00:20:55,933 --> 00:20:57,567
- [TEKLA] I'll be your partner.
- Put them all inside!

432
00:20:57,567 --> 00:20:59,067
- [BINOY] Take the comforter!
- Get to work!

433
00:20:59,067 --> 00:21:01,067
- [IPE] Yes, sir.
- Do that first, okay?

434
00:21:01,067 --> 00:21:03,733
- Hurry up a little.
- Don't forget the comforter!

435
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:04,900
- [TEKLA] Bye!
- Bring it in!

436
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,967
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

437
00:21:06,967 --> 00:21:08,233
I got nervous there.

438
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,600
- Where do we put this?
- [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

439
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,233
- Excuse me.
- Right here!

440
00:21:11,233 --> 00:21:13,667
- I'll try that on.
- I really like this one.

441
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:15,067
- Can we take this home?
- Hey!

442
00:21:15,067 --> 00:21:16,733
Stop playing around!

443
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:18,000
Let me think.

444
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,433
- Grab these!
- Huh?

445
00:21:19,433 --> 00:21:20,933
- Come on, we'll pretend--
- Black?

446
00:21:20,933 --> 00:21:22,067
We'll pretend to be waiters!

447
00:21:22,067 --> 00:21:24,233
- I'll just be bossed around!
- Drop the diva act!

448
00:21:24,233 --> 00:21:25,400
- Or you'll see!
- Where's mine?

449
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,900
It's an all-black outfit.
Just lose the extras!

450
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:29,600
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

451
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:33,467
[CROWD CHEERING]

452
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:54,567
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

453
00:22:08,867 --> 00:22:15,867
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

454
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:34,033
- [MUSIC BECOMES UPBEAT]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

455
00:22:36,067 --> 00:22:40,600
[CROWD CHEERING]

456
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:48,900
[WHOOPING, CHEERING]

457
00:22:48,933 --> 00:22:54,867
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

458
00:23:03,900 --> 00:23:06,367
- Bye, handsome!
- [MAN] Bye, miss!

459
00:23:06,367 --> 00:23:08,267
[BINOY] Hey, remember
to separate the colors!

460
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,333
- [FIRE FLARING]
- [CHEF] My goodness!

461
00:23:11,333 --> 00:23:13,967
What the heck is this?
We've got tons of clients!

462
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:15,267
They've been waiting
for the food!

463
00:23:15,267 --> 00:23:16,833
Any update on the sea bass,
the salmon?

464
00:23:16,833 --> 00:23:18,033
Where's the garnish?

465
00:23:18,033 --> 00:23:20,367
Hurry up!
What a bunch of slowpokes!

466
00:23:20,367 --> 00:23:22,367
My goodness!
Focus on your stations!

467
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,933
All of you! Stop bunching up!
Pick up the pace!

468
00:23:24,933 --> 00:23:26,367
You, come here! I need you here!

469
00:23:26,367 --> 00:23:27,667
- [CHEF] Move faster!
- She wants you!

470
00:23:27,667 --> 00:23:28,967
- Yes, you! Come here!
- Go, go!

471
00:23:28,967 --> 00:23:30,500
Come on, hurry up!

472
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:31,967
Top these with icing now!

473
00:23:31,967 --> 00:23:33,133
- Hurry!
- Yes, Chef!

474
00:23:33,133 --> 00:23:34,333
You, come here!

475
00:23:34,333 --> 00:23:35,833
- Me? What?
- Work on these vegetables!

476
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:37,000
- Huh?
- My goodness!

477
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,300
We're still missing garnish!

478
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:40,533
- What do I do?
- Blanch them and chop them!

479
00:23:40,533 --> 00:23:42,400
- Where do I put these?
- Geez, are you new here?

480
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,467
Put them over there!

481
00:23:43,467 --> 00:23:44,567
Go, start chopping!

482
00:23:44,567 --> 00:23:46,433
You, clean up the mess here!

483
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:47,900
The three of you! Hurry!

484
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,067
- She meant us.
- Here!

485
00:23:49,067 --> 00:23:50,900
Serve those to Table 3!

486
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,300
- Come on, hurry!
- O-Okay, okay!

487
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:53,333
Walk that way!

488
00:23:53,333 --> 00:23:54,500
- You two!
- Yes?

489
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:55,667
Make sure the customers
get them!

490
00:23:55,700 --> 00:23:56,967
Move faster!
We've got tons of guests!

491
00:23:56,967 --> 00:23:58,600
[UPBEAT MUSIC RESUMES]

492
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:00,267
[GUEST CHEERING]

493
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:02,933
[BODIES THUD]

494
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:06,233
- You okay?
- Sorry.

495
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:07,900
Just chill, okay?

496
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:09,333
Sorry again, dude.

497
00:24:09,333 --> 00:24:10,867
[CROWD CHEERING]

498
00:24:12,833 --> 00:24:19,333
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

499
00:24:19,333 --> 00:24:21,000
[WOMEN WHOOPING]

500
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:27,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

501
00:24:32,267 --> 00:24:33,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

502
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:34,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

503
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:36,933
We're almost there.
We have the item.

504
00:24:39,433 --> 00:24:41,867
Mr. Chan,
I'll meet them downstairs.

505
00:24:42,167 --> 00:24:43,900
Okay. I'll wait here.

506
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:48,900
Don't let other people in.

507
00:24:49,167 --> 00:24:50,367
[BODYGUARD] Yes, ma'am.

508
00:24:50,367 --> 00:24:53,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

509
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:55,167
[CROWD CHEERING]

510
00:24:55,167 --> 00:24:59,267
[UPBEAT MUSIC RESUMES]

511
00:24:59,267 --> 00:25:00,833
[CROWD WHOOPING]

512
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:19,333
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

513
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:21,567
See? We made it to the party!

514
00:25:25,667 --> 00:25:27,733
Why are you dancing?
We're waiters here!

515
00:25:27,733 --> 00:25:29,267
Oh, right.

516
00:25:29,267 --> 00:25:30,233
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

517
00:25:30,900 --> 00:25:32,567
I've been looking for you.

518
00:25:32,567 --> 00:25:34,900
Bring to this Mr. Chan
upstairs in the VIP room.

519
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:38,133
- Hurry up.
- Okay, sir.

520
00:25:38,133 --> 00:25:45,133
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

521
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:50,900
Gabo! Gabo!

522
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:52,733
Well?

523
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,300
Have you seen Mr. Chan?

524
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:56,400
Oh, Mr. Chan?
He's in the VIP room.

525
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:57,900
I'm actually bringing
this alcohol to him.

526
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,567
See if the Tiger has arrived
and let us know.

527
00:26:01,567 --> 00:26:02,700
Okay, I'll keep you updated.

528
00:26:02,700 --> 00:26:03,733
Wait here.

529
00:26:05,733 --> 00:26:06,900
Gabo.

530
00:26:06,900 --> 00:26:09,067
Are you really sure
about this job?

531
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:11,100
I'm worried.

532
00:26:11,100 --> 00:26:13,700
Looks like they're
a big-time syndicate.

533
00:26:13,700 --> 00:26:15,600
I just hope
the money's worth it.

534
00:26:16,067 --> 00:26:17,767
Our lives could be
at stake, Gabo!

535
00:26:19,133 --> 00:26:21,167
I told you not to come along,

536
00:26:21,167 --> 00:26:22,467
but you insisted.

537
00:26:22,467 --> 00:26:24,033
I-It's not like that!

538
00:26:24,033 --> 00:26:26,167
You know we need money, too.

539
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:28,733
It just doesn't feel right.
They're heavily armed,

540
00:26:28,733 --> 00:26:30,633
while we're coming in
empty-handed.

541
00:26:30,633 --> 00:26:33,067
Why be scared?
We've got Gabo!

542
00:26:33,067 --> 00:26:34,667
He can handle them no problem!

543
00:26:34,667 --> 00:26:37,533
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

544
00:26:37,533 --> 00:26:38,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

545
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:40,867
Sir, here's the bottle
of special alcohol you ordered--

546
00:26:40,867 --> 00:26:42,333
- Put it there!
- Okay.

547
00:26:42,367 --> 00:26:45,100
[BOTTLE, GLASS THUD]

548
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:49,633
Sir, are you alone?
No one's with you?

549
00:26:51,767 --> 00:26:53,500
None of your business! Go!

550
00:26:53,500 --> 00:26:55,433
- Oh, s-sorry...
- Go, go!

551
00:26:55,433 --> 00:26:56,467
I'm going.

552
00:26:58,633 --> 00:27:01,600
[CROWD CHEERING]

553
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:02,800
[TOLITS] Gabo! Gabo!

554
00:27:03,533 --> 00:27:05,400
So, is the Tiger inside or what?

555
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:06,567
Negative.

556
00:27:06,567 --> 00:27:08,233
Only Mr. Chan's in the room.

557
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:11,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

558
00:27:11,133 --> 00:27:13,900
You guys stay downstairs.

559
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:15,433
I'll wait up here.

560
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:18,000
As soon as the Tiger shows up,
signal me immediately.

561
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,233
- Now, go!
- Okay, sure!

562
00:27:19,233 --> 00:27:20,867
- Let's go, let's go!
- See you around.

563
00:27:20,867 --> 00:27:25,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

564
00:27:27,067 --> 00:27:32,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

565
00:27:32,367 --> 00:27:36,733
[CAR ENGINES REVVING]

566
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,333
[BRAKE SQUEALS]

567
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:55,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

568
00:27:57,900 --> 00:28:04,800
[CLUB MUSIC BLARING]

569
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:11,367
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

570
00:28:16,700 --> 00:28:19,267
Sir, Mr. Chan
is waiting for you.

571
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:21,067
Let's not keep him waiting.

572
00:28:25,133 --> 00:28:32,100
[CLUB MUSIC CONTINUES BLARING]

573
00:28:51,333 --> 00:28:58,300
[CLUB MUSIC CONTINUES BLARING]

574
00:29:21,267 --> 00:29:28,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

575
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:57,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

576
00:30:19,833 --> 00:30:22,167
<i> Tiger is the leader</i>

577
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:27,200
<i>of the biggest gold smuggling
syndicate in the country.</i>

578
00:30:27,333 --> 00:30:30,567
<i>They have gold bars
and millions of money inside!</i>

579
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:31,767
There's just a bit of a problem.

580
00:30:31,900 --> 00:30:33,500
<i>He's got tons of
armed bodyguards.</i>

581
00:30:33,633 --> 00:30:35,900
<i>Trying to capture him now
is basically suicide.</i>

582
00:30:36,067 --> 00:30:37,900
Victor Zafra, hands in the air!

583
00:30:38,033 --> 00:30:40,000
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [BODY THUDS]

584
00:30:40,133 --> 00:30:42,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

585
00:30:42,833 --> 00:30:44,600
[GUNSHOTS]

586
00:30:44,733 --> 00:30:47,933
<i> I need backup!
</i>Send them to Twin Phoenix! Now!

587
00:30:48,067 --> 00:30:49,600
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

588
00:30:49,733 --> 00:30:52,500
<i>- Don't let them catch you!
- I know! Shut up!</i>

589
00:30:52,633 --> 00:30:54,800
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARS]

590
00:30:58,333 --> 00:30:59,633
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GLASS SHATTERS]

591
00:30:59,767 --> 00:31:01,333
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

592
00:31:01,467 --> 00:31:03,033
[BRAKES, TIRES SQUEALING]

593
00:31:03,167 --> 00:31:04,033
[BLOWS LAND]

594
00:31:04,167 --> 00:31:06,100
- [GLASS SHATTERS]
- [KICKS LAND]

595
00:31:06,233 --> 00:31:07,433
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]

596
00:31:07,567 --> 00:31:09,433
[LOUD CRASH]

597
00:31:11,967 --> 00:31:13,933
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]
